<title>CHINA: China Exim bank makes $9.62 mln forest loan.</title>
<headline>China Exim bank makes $9.62 mln forest loan.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Import and Export Bank of China has loaned $9.62 million to a local company to develop forest resources and produce timber in Papua New Guinea, state television said on Friday.</p>
<p>The loan was made to the Jilin Forest Industrial Group, which has taken a 30-year lease on 120,000 hectares of forest in Papua New Guinea, Chinese Central Television said.</p>
<p>The company plans to produce 100,000 cubic metres of timber each year, it said, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
